Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 20:04:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 050/154] feat: the /settings route, its shell and its message
 names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A module, a ROUTES entry, two names in kSurfaceMessages and two .grd entries.
The panes themselves come next; this is the shape they hang on.

A selection carries the pane's own id, never its position in the rail, so a
rail reordered later cannot change what a stored or in-flight selection means.
An unknown id falls back to the first pane rather than rendering an empty
frame.

Built against DOM APIs rather than markup strings - the WebUI CSP forbids
innerHTML, and a surface that will grow fields holding user data should not
start with the wrong habit.

The .grd allocation had to widen from 20 includes to 30. Two more entries
overflowed it and grit fails the build rather than silently reassigning ids.

Verified by six DOM tests, and by the suite as a whole: 478 tests, up from
472, and webui-verify reports 32 chrome.send names all registered, up from 30.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec b/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
index b0f961a49004b..3d2d5aefb2b9b 100644
--- a/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
+++ b/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
@@ -1810,7 +1810,7 @@
   # Atrium chrome layer. Placed at the end of this section so the
   # real IDs land after the placeholder block and nothing downstream realigns.
   "chrome/browser/resources/atrium/atrium_resources.grd": {
-    "META": {"sizes": {"includes": [20]}},
+    "META": {"sizes": {"includes": [30]}},
     "includes": [12020],
   },
 
